<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Francesco Mario Pagano</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1748–1799</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Francesco Mario Pagano was a Neapolitan jurist and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/age-of-enlightenment">Enlightenment</a> philosopher, author of the Saggi politici. A leader of the Parthenopean Republic of 1799, he drafted its constitution, which drew on French models but added an assembly of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ephor">ephors</a> to guard it. When the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-bourbon">Bourbon</a> monarchy was restored that summer he was executed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> with other republican leaders.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/francesco-mario-pagano.jpg" alt="Francesco Mario Pagano" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Parmiani · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mario_Pagano.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
